{
  "policy_type": "rules",
  "name": "policy_ep_40",
  "rules": [
    {
      "if": [
        {"feature": "vy", "op": "<", "value": -0.5},
        {"feature": "theta", "op": ">", "value": -0.1},
        {"feature": "theta", "op": "<", "value": 0.1}
      ],
      "then": 2
    },
    {
      "if": [
        {"feature": "vx", "op": ">", "value": 0.5},
        {"feature": "theta", "op": ">", "value": 0}
      ],
      "then": 3
    },
    {
      "if": [
        {"feature": "vx", "op": "<", "value": -0.5},
        {"feature": "theta", "op": "<", "value": 0}
      ],
      "then": 1
    },
    {
      "if": [
        {"feature": "left_leg", "op": "==", "value": 1},
        {"feature": "right_leg", "op": "==", "value": 1}
      ],
      "then": 0
    }
  ],
  "default_action": 0,
  "notes": "This new policy is influenced by the need to improve landing stability and reduce crash rates. The previous policy had an average return of 50 with 70% coverage in successful landing scenarios. The modifications focus on enhancing the response to vertical and horizontal velocities, as well as the lander angle, which were identified as critical factors in the greedy evaluation trajectories. The rules were adjusted to prioritize firing the main engine for gentle descent while ensuring the orientation engines are activated when necessary to correct horizontal movement." 
}

